{"id":"src/lib/hospital/opdData.ts","pkg":"src/lib/hospital","kind":"module","lines":165,"commentLines":27,"header":["The hospital data (step 51a). I keep it in two JSON files so that it can grow without touching code: data/hospital_staff.json -- the people of the hospital (doctors and other staff), linked to the intranet doctor list and the roster data/opd_schedule.json -- OPD timings, the closure rules, and for every department its OPD units with the doctor (or state) of every weekday Important: both files come from lists the hospital gave on 24 Oct 2026 that are not up to date (retired doctors are still in them), so every answer says so. To add or correct data later, edit the JSON: when a doctor leaves, set \"status\"; for a new unit, add it to its department; when a head or an HOD becomes known, set \"head\" / \"hod\"."],"symbols":[{"name":"Weekday","kind":"type","exported":true,"line":13,"generics":"","sig":"\"MON\" | \"TUE\" | \"WED\" | \"THU\" | \"FRI\" | \"SAT\" | \"SUN\"","doc":[],"id":"1d65f77da7-Weekday","usedBy":["src/lib/hospital/dates.ts","src/lib/hospital/engine.ts","src/lib/search/pureAiEngine.ts"]},{"name":"OPD_DAYS","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":15,"sig":"const OPD_DAYS: Weekday[] = [\"MON\", \"TUE\", \"WED\", \"THU\", \"FRI\", \"SAT\"]","type":"Weekday[]","doc":["I list the six OPD days in the order of the schedule."],"members":[],"items":6,"id":"1d65f77da7-OPD_DAYS","usedBy":["src/lib/hospital/engine.ts","src/lib/search/pureAiEngine.ts"]},{"name":"WEEKDAY_NAME","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":16,"sig":"const WEEKDAY_NAME: Record<Weekday, string> = { MON: \"Monday\", TUE: \"Tuesday\", WED: \"Wednesday\", THU: \"Thursday\", FRI: \"Friday\", SAT: \"Saturday\", SUN: \"Sunday\" }","type":"Record<Weekday, string>","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"key","name":"MON","line":16,"value":"\"Monday\"","doc":[]},{"kind":"key","name":"TUE","line":16,"value":"\"Tuesday\"","doc":[]},{"kind":"key","name":"WED","line":16,"value":"\"Wednesday\"","doc